In ePumpAP/example directory, some examples are provided for instructing how to prepare input files for ePump running.

To run the PDF only update with C++ executable, usage,

UpdatePDF test

To run the PDF + alpha_s update with C++ executable, usage,

UpdatePDF test testAlphaS

####################################################################################################################################################

Here is an instruction for using the Python interface of the new ePump code.

An example is prepared in the following place:

ePumpAP/src/ePumpHelper/PythonExt/UpdatePDFs.py

First, the object needs to be initialized,

ep = PyePump.PyePump()
ep.Initialize("test")

Here we provide a function to specify the draw list of LM scan plot. Note that the BaseName which is the name of your directory saving all .data and .theory files should be there,

BaseName = "tabsCT18Am248_1164/"
LMScanDrawList = [BaseName + "E160",
                  BaseName + "E542",
                  BaseName + "E545",
                  BaseName + "E544",
                  BaseName + "E514",
                  BaseName + "E504",
                  BaseName + "E147",
                  BaseName + "E102",
                  BaseName + "E101",
                  BaseName + "E110",
                  BaseName + "E248",]

ep.InputLMScanDrawList(LMScanDrawList)

The main function for PDF only update,

ep.Update()

The main function for PDF + alpha_s update. Note that this should be called after calling Update()

ep.UpdateAlphaS("testAlphaS")

The LM scan module for specific PDF flavor, x, and Q,

# PDFLMScanModule(int flavor, double x, double Q, int isUpdate)
ep.PDFLMScanModule(0, 0.01, 125.0, 0)
ep.PDFLMScanModule(0, 0.01, 125.0, 1)

The LM scan module for AlphaS,

# UpdateAlphaSLMScanPDF(int flavor, double x, double Q)
ep.UpdateAlphaSLMScanPDF(0, 0.01, 125.0)

The correlation ellipse plot production between any observable you provide and alpha_s,

# AlphaSObservableCorrelation(const char* name, int iPoint, const char* legend)
ep.AlphaSObservableCorrelation(BaseName + "ggHiggsXsec", 0, "#sigma(gg #rightarrow H) [pb]")

Other useful functions to obtain the meta output from the ePump,

ep.GetOldTheory(BaseName + "ggHiggsXsec", 0)
ep.GetNewTheory(BaseName + "ggHiggsXsec", 0)
ep.GetOldPDFError(BaseName + "ggHiggsXsec", 0)
ep.GetNewPDFError(BaseName + "ggHiggsXsec", 0)
ep.GetOldPDFCorrelation(DataName1, DataName2, i, j)
ep.GetNewPDFCorrelation(DataName1, DataName2, i, j)
ep.GetOldChi2(DataName)
ep.GetNewChi2(DataName)
ep.GetOldAlphaS()
ep.GetNewAlphaS()
ep.GetOldAlphaSError()
ep.GetNewAlphaSError()

